The <ansi fg="command">knowledge</ansi> command inspects and manipulates NPC
knowledge records written by the chunk-1.4 knowledge substrate.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Usage:</ansi>

<ansi fg="command">knowledge show <mobId></ansi>
  List all knowledge records held by this observer NPC, sorted by
  most-recently-seen first.

<ansi fg="command">knowledge show <mobId> <playerName></ansi>
  Show this observer's full knowledge record for one player —
  HasMet, name, source, confidence, last-seen room, and any
  witnessed crimes.

<ansi fg="command">knowledge show <mobId> mob <targetId></ansi>
  Same as above, but for an NPC target (numeric template id).

<ansi fg="command">knowledge frequented <mobId> <playerName> [topK]</ansi>
  List the top-K rooms where this observer has seen the player,
  tallied from the bounded observation log. Default topK is 5.

<ansi fg="command">knowledge forget <mobId> <playerName></ansi>
  Drop the entire knowledge record for that player from this
  observer's file.

<ansi fg="command">knowledge forget <mobId> <playerName> <fact></ansi>
  Drop a single fact from the record. Valid facts:
    name         — clear the learned name
    observations — clear the observation log
    crimes       — clear witnessed crime ids

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Notes:</ansi>
  - <mobId> accepts a numeric template id or a mob name
    (matched via ConvertForFilename, e.g. "lars" or "smith").
  - Storage: _datafiles/world/dogmud/knowledge/<mobId>-<name>.yaml
    (gitignored runtime state).
  - Forget is immediate and persisted to disk; reloading the server
    will not restore forgotten records.
